@startuml

start

:Power management subsystem governed by RTOS;
:Continuously monitor voltage rails via PMIC and BMS;
:Execute protection policies within dedicated high-priority task;

if (Signal strength < defined threshold?) then (yes)
  :Query battery state;
  if (Sufficient charge?) then (yes)
    :Initiate signal compensation routine;
  else (no)
    fork
    :Enter low-power mode;
    fork again
    :Watchdog service dispatch priority-queued warning to central control via CAN bus;
    end fork
  end if
else (no)
end if

fork
  :Data acquisition sampled via timer ISRs;
  :Debounce;
fork again
  :Uplink transmission task execute under the RTOS scheduler;
  :Write telemetry and device status reports to ring buffer;
fork again
  :Lower-priority telemetry task persistently observes network link;
  if (Detect failure?) then (yes)
    :Trigger reconnection mechanism;
    :Employ;
    fork
    :Exponential backoff;
    fork again
    :CRC-verified link-state probing;
    end fork
  :Resume normal throughput;
  else (no)
  end if
end fork

:Capture in structured audit log;
fork
:Fault information;
fork again
:Operational state transitions;
end fork

:Flush to non-volatile storage under strict I/O budget;
:Upload system status summary;
:Analysis following staged recovery and verification cycles;

stop

@enduml
